Alice: Haha. Yeah, me too. I really like to play, but I never bet money. :)

Bob: Oh, I never bet money on Big Two either. Except for that one time a few weeks ago.

Alice: A few weeks ago, what happened?

Bob: I went to a friend's house. He wanted to play Big Two, so I said okay. Then he said one cent per card, because he's really good. So I thought, "Why not?" Besides, the most I could lose was about ten dollars.

Alice: That's true. :) Hehe. Your friend is pretty good at it. It's actually good, but if I really had to bet money, I wouldn't enjoy the game as much.

Bob: But it's not good to be too serious about it. Yeah, if you have to bet money, it's really stressful. By the way, do you have the program?

Alice: What program? No. Do I need to download it or something? :)

Bob: Well, to play online, you need a program. My client doesn't support file transfers yet. Maybe you can get it from me through FTP or HTTP. Wait...

Alice: Okay. :) Thank you. Hehe. [end of text]


